        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000058</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A high-carbon version of 321 SS with improved creep strength and rupture strength at high temperatures. It is used for pressure vessels and boilers1</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>321H SS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000059 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000059">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000059</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An austenitic stainless steel with columbium (or niobium) added to stabilize it against intergranular corrosion. It has similar properties to 321 SS but can withstand higher temperatures up to 900°C5</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>347 SS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000060 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000060">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000060</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A high-carbon version of 347 SS with enhanced creep strength and rupture strength at high temperatures. It is used for superheaters, reheaters and steam pipes6</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>347H SS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000061 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000061">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000061</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A low-alloy steel with chromium and molybdenum as the main alloying elements. It has good corrosion resistance and high-temperature strength. It is used for pressure vessels and boilers7</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>3CR-1MO</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000062 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000062">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000062</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A low-alloy steel with chromium, molybdenum and vanadium as the main alloying elements. It has better creep resistance and rupture strength than 3CR-1MO. It is used for steam generators and nuclear reactors. [No results found]</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>3CR-1MO-V</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000063 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000063">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000063</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A duplex stainless steel with a balanced mixture of austenite and ferrite phases. It has high strength, good corrosion resistance and good weldability. It is used for chemical tankers, pulp and paper industry, and seawater applications. [No results found]</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>3RE60 (18.5Cr-5Ni)</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000064 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000064">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000048"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000064</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <rdfs:label>400</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000065 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000065">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000065</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A ferritic stainless steel with lower chromium content than 430 SS. It has good weldability and moderate corrosion resistance. It is used for steam nozzles, quenching racks, annealing boxes and other high-temperature applications. [No results found]</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>405 SS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000066 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000066">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000066</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A martensitic stainless steel with high hardness and moderate corrosion resistance. It can be hardened by heat treatment and has good mechanical properties. It is used for cutlery, surgical instruments, valves, pumps, turbines and more8</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>410 SS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000067 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000067">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000067</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A martensitic stainless steel with higher nickel content than 410 SS. It has better toughness and corrosion resistance than 410 SS but lower hardness and strength. It is used for fasteners, fittings, gears, shafts and more. [No results found]</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>414 SS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000068 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000068">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000068</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A free-machining variation of martensitic stainless steel with added sulphur or selenium for improved machinability. It has lower corrosion resistance than 410 SS but higher strength and hardness after heat treatment. It is used for nuts, bolts, screws, gears, shafts and more9</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>416 SS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000069 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000069">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000131"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000069</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <rdfs:label>4-20 mA</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000070 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000070">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000131"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000070</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <rdfs:label>4-20 mA HART</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000071 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000071">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000071</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A ferritic stainless steel with lower chromium content than 430 SS. It has good formability and weldability but lower corrosion resistance than 430 SS. It is used for automotive exhaust systems, catalytic converters, mufflers and more10</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>429 SS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000072 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000072">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000072</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A ferritic stainless steel with good corrosion resistance in mildly corrosive environments and good oxidation resistance at elevated temperatures. It has good formability and ductility but cannot be hardened by heat treatment. It is used for appliances, cookware, flatware, automotive trim and more11</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>430 SS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000073 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000073">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000073</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A ferritic stainless steel with higher chromium content than 430 SS. It has better scaling resistance at high temperatures and better corrosion resistance in sulphurous gases than 430 SS. It is used for furnace parts, heat exchangers, burners and more12</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>442 SS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000074 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000074">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000074</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A ferritic stainless steel with very high chromium content that provides excellent resistance to oxidation and corrosion at high temperatures. It has good mechanical properties but poor ductility and weldability. It is used for furnace parts, radiant tubes, thermocouple tubes and more13</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>446 SS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000076 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000076">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000076</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A low-alloy steel with chromium and molybdenum as the main alloying elements. It has good corrosion resistance and high-temperature strength. It is used for pressure vessels, boilers, heat exchangers, piping and more. [No results found]</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>5 CR - 0.5 MO</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000077 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000077">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000077</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A low-alloy steel with chromium, molybdenum and silicon as the main alloying elements. It has better creep resistance and rupture strength than 5 CR - 0.5 MO. It is used for steam generators, nuclear reactors, superheaters and more. [No results found]</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>5 CR - 0.5 MO-SI</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000078 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000078">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000048"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000078</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <rdfs:label>5000</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000079 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000079">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-50000073"/>
        <hasCFIHOSCode>CFIHOS-60000079</hasCFIHOSCode>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A high-alloy steel with equal amounts of chromium and nickel as the main alloying elements. It has excellent resistance to oxidation and carburization at high temperatures. It is used for furnace parts, radiant tubes, thermocouple tubes and more. [No results found]</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>50CR-50NI</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000080 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://infohub.siemens-energy.com/CFIHOS#CFIHOS-60000080">
